      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Write $\\frac{7{x}^{2}+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{7{x}^{2}-x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$7{x}^{2}+11$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\" align=\"center\">$=$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\" align=\"center\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}} \n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$7{x}^{2}-x$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$7{x}^{2}-x$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, we add and subtract $x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}\\,=\\,\\frac{7{x}^{2}-x+x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}-x+x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x} & =\\frac{7{x}^{2}-x}{7{x}^{2}-x}+\\frac{x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
